WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.619
When a grid looks wrong, it's
usually doing what it was told,

2
00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:05.649
in an order you didn't expect.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.190
Today: that order, on the Quarter View,
and a switch that shows every cell.

4
00:00:10.403 --> 00:00:12.233
I'll click April's calendar.

5
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:16.367
As in episode 7, its steps run
in the order they're listed.

6
00:00:16.418 --> 00:00:19.694
The source and Deep
Traversal find April's days,

7
00:00:19.694 --> 00:00:22.901
Final Data Subset, empty
here, would trim them,

8
00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.925
and the offset comes last.

9
00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:28.272
April starts on a Wednesday,
so two blank cells.

10
00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:30.206
Here's a mistake I've made.

11
00:00:30.245 --> 00:00:35.234
I want this calendar to show the next
month, and Final Data Subset sounds right:

12
00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.545
Start Index, one.

13
00:00:36.757 --> 00:00:38.997
It's still April, minus the first.

14
00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:43.327
The subset runs after traversal,
so it trimmed a day, not a month.

15
00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.254
Did the offset change too?

16
00:00:45.424 --> 00:00:49.195
The second stayed under Thursday,
but blank cells don't show here,

17
00:00:49.195 --> 00:00:51.044
so there's nothing to count.

18
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.800
Empty Cell Borders, under
Grid Formatting, draws them.

19
00:00:54.879 --> 00:00:58.322
It needs a real cell border
first, and as in episode 4,

20
00:00:58.322 --> 00:01:01.639
the color and width shown
here are only borrowed.

21
00:01:02.368 --> 00:01:04.988
So: a gray, half a point, and the switch.

22
00:01:05.127 --> 00:01:06.767
Three empty cells now.

23
00:01:06.881 --> 00:01:10.511
The offset re-read the first
day left, Thursday the second.

24
00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.210
The slice ran first.

25
00:01:12.424 --> 00:01:14.814
Picking a month is traversal's job.

26
00:01:14.923 --> 00:01:18.423
Clear the subset, and give the
first level a Start of one.

27
00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:20.379
That's May.

28
00:01:20.511 --> 00:01:23.494
It starts on a Friday,
so four bordered blanks:

29
00:01:23.494 --> 00:01:26.981
a first row that's mostly
empty, for a good reason.

30
00:01:27.201 --> 00:01:30.251
Back to zero, and April's
offset is two again.

31
00:01:31.495 --> 00:01:33.775
Borders help with a blank grid too.

32
00:01:33.921 --> 00:01:37.870
A typo in Display Template,
day_number instead of day_num,

33
00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.891
and every cell goes empty.

34
00:01:40.097 --> 00:01:44.607
The cells are all still there, so the steps
above are fine; it's what they print.

35
00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.221
Fix the name, and the numbers come back.

36
00:01:47.428 --> 00:01:50.628
So: traversal, then the
subset, then the offset.

37
00:01:50.673 --> 00:01:54.249
The export runs the same steps,
and the borders print too,

38
00:01:54.249 --> 00:01:56.223
so keep them or switch them off.
